:: Farm Bus to Farm [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
<<set $Money -= 3>>
Stepping onto the bus, you ask the driver if it’ll take you out towards the farms on the eastern side of town. The man nods, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Yup, we’ll take you o’er there!”</span> He has a thick accent, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Take a ‘sec to get there, but we do have a stop. ‘ave a seat!”</span> You thank the man and take a seat. <br>
<br>
The bus is pretty empty at the moment, and you stare idly out of the window as people get on and off at the various stops around town. Finally, the bus pulls off from the High School towards the farms. At this point only a pair of old men, a tired looking teenager in a store uniform, and young woman are on the bus. This collection of tired and older folks leaves the ride out to the farms almost completely quiet outside of the light dim of the radio. You nearly fall asleep by the time you feel the bus come to a stop. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Opal City Country Side, next stop, Preston High School!”</span> He announces as you and the rest of the passengers unload. Two new people get on from this stop, but the bus is empty outside of them as it pulls away, leaving you standing at the bus stop in the large, near-empty field with a few scattered farmhouses around. Welp, time to do what you came here for. <br>
<br>
[[Continue|Farm]]


:: Farm Bus to Town [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 15>>
<<set $Money -= 3>>
You are waiting at the bus stop for what seems like forever when you finally see the large blue vehicle crest over the hill and come towards you. Despite knowing the bus always arrives on time, you still found yourself a little worried that something went wrong and you’d have to walk home. Only two people get off, and you find the bus completely empty as you pay the driver and take your seat. <br>
<br>
The ride back would have been in complete silence had the man not turned up the radio to break it. You find yourself thankful for this, as the silence on this deserted road would have been kind of eerie. The subtle sounds of the radio mixed with the seemingly endless stretches of farmland and deserted fields makes for an extremely relaxing trip back. <br>
<br>
Though this quickly ends as soon as he gets back into the town proper, as more people file on and take their seats. The bus gets pretty full by the time you arrive at your destination, and you find yourself happy to get off. <br>
<br>
[[Continue|Farm]]